<article class="env-definition" id="21FD55">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/21FD55">Definition <span data-tag="21FD55">8.2.6.2</span>.</a>$\kappa $-accessible subcategoryaccessible!subcategory Let $\calC $ be a presentable category and $\kappa $ a regular cardinal. We will say that a full subcategory $\calC _0 \subseteq \calC $ is an <em>$\kappa $-accessible subcategory</em> of $\calC $ if the following conditions are satisfied: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The full subcategory $\calC _0 \subseteq \calC $ is stable under $\kappa $-filtered colimits. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
There exists a (small) set of objects of $\calC _0$ which generates $\calC _0$ under $\kappa $-filtered colimits. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
  <p> We will say that $\calC _0 \subseteq \calC $ is an <em>accessible subcategory</em> if $\calC _0$ is a $\kappa $-accessible subcategory of $\calC $, for some regular cardinal $\kappa $. </p>
</article>